    "chunk_text": "\u201cBig boss or boss\u2019s son - It doesn\u2019t matter\u201d - President\n\nColombo, Sep. 13 (Daily Mirror) - President Anura Kumara Dissanayake has pledged to continue an uncompromising crackdown on corruption, drug trafficking and organized crime, while outlining a series of development and welfare measures for rural communities.\n\nAddressing a National People\u2019s Power (NPP) rally in Nochchiyagama, the President said there were no political threats facing his government and that the rallies were aimed at building a strong public movement to transform the country\u2019s economic, social and political systems.\n\nHe said the mandate received by the NPP on September 21, 2024, had brought an end to traditional political practices, including VIP privileges, excessive security arrangements and dynastic politics.\n\nPresident Dissanayake said that law enforcement and investigative institutions had been given the independence necessary to carry out their duties without political interference.\n\n\u201cA small, primitive group of people says, \u2018It\u2019s okay if they stole, but don\u2019t send them to prison.\u2019 Is there such a thing? Should we allow that? No, remember that. Some people still say, \u2018Our thief is good for us.\u2019 That small, remaining group is all that is left.\n\n\u201cThose who go after corrupt people, those who say corrupt individuals should not be punished, and those who say they should not be sent to prison\u2014they are not everywhere. They represent only a tiny fraction of the country.\n\n\u201cAs the President, I am standing here blindfolded. I don\u2019t see who the thief is; it is not relevant to me. Who the corrupt person is\u2014it is not relevant to me. Is he a big boss, the boss\u2019s son, the boss\u2019s wife or the boss\u2019s mother-in-law? Does that matter to us?"
  },
