    "chunk_text": "\u201cAs the President, I am standing here blindfolded. I don\u2019t see who the thief is; it is not relevant to me. Who the corrupt person is\u2014it is not relevant to me. Is he a big boss, the boss\u2019s son, the boss\u2019s wife or the boss\u2019s mother-in-law? Does that matter to us?\n\nResponding to calls from the opposition to place limits on corruption investigations, he said the government would not impose restrictions on investigations into corrupt politicians, drug networks or underworld groups.\n\n\"About seven or eight months ago, people asked, 'Why aren't you arresting anyone?' They asked, 'Where are the file caches you talked about?' Now what are they asking? I saw a former minister saying that there should be a limit to arresting thieves. Is there a limit to arresting thieves? No, catching thieves is unlimited,\" the President said.\n\nHe said that no individual would be protected because of political status or position and that investigations would continue regardless of who was involved.\n\nTurning to development in the North Central Province, the President highlighted several major infrastructure projects. He said more than Rs. 50 billion had been allocated for the Kebithigollewa water project, while over Rs. 47 billion had been allocated for the Lower Malwathu Oya reservoir project.\n\nHe also said the government had allocated Rs. 18.5 billion for the purchase of paddy."
