    "chunk_size_bytes": 1836,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka\u2013Indonesia Business Council holds 3rd Annual General Meeting\n\nCeylon Biscuits Chairman/Group Managing Director Sheamalee Wickramasingha was re-elected Council President for 2026/27\n\nChief Guest, Indonesian Ambassador to Sri Lanka Dewi Gustina Tobing\n\nThe Sri Lanka\u2013Indonesia Business Council of The Ceylon Chamber of Commerce held its 3rd Annual General Meeting recently,\u00a0 bringing together Council members and key stakeholders to review the Council\u2019s activities and priorities for the year ahead.\n\nThe AGM was graced by Ambassador of Indonesia to Sri Lanka and Patron of the Council Dewi Gustina Tobing.\n\nDelivering her address, Dewi Gustina Tobing, Ambassador of Indonesia to Sri Lanka, provided a comprehensive overview of Indonesia\u2019s political and economic landscape, highlighting the country\u2019s focus on promoting economic independence, strengthening sectoral resilience, improving public welfare, and facilitating both inbound and outbound investment.\n\nRe-elected as President of the Council for 2026/27,\u00a0 Ceylon Biscuits Ltd., Chairman/Group Managing Director Sheamalee Wickramasingha, acknowledged the instrumental role played by the Ambassador in the re-establishment of the Council and reflected on the Council\u2019s key achievements during the past year. She\u00a0 highlighted the successful Sri Lanka\u2013Indonesia Business Delegation to Indonesia, which provided valuable opportunities for Sri Lankan businesses to engage with Indonesian counterparts and explore avenues for commercial cooperation. The\u00a0 office bearers for the 2026/2027 term include Senior Vice President\u00a0 - Gerard Victoria, Director/CEO North South Lines Ltd.,\u00a0 Vice President -\u00a0 Ehantha Sirisena, Founder/Director OMAK Technologies Ltd.,\u00a0 and Treasurer - Marshad Barry, Deputy Head of Orphan Care & Institutional Marketing of Amana Bank."
  },
