    "chunk_size_bytes": 1901,
    "chunk_text": "Dearo Venture Capital strengthens leadership, unveils strategic vision for SL\u2019s economic growth\n\nDearo Venture Capital Ltd, Sri Lanka\u2019s largest venture capital institution, officially announced the appointment of its new Director Board at a special media conference held on 10 September.\n\nThe event brought together members of the media, business leaders, investors, stakeholders, and members of the Dearo management team to witness the unveiling of the company\u2019s renewed strategic direction and long-term vision for supporting entrepreneurship and economic development in Sri Lanka.\n\nThe newly appointed Board of Directors comprises professionals with extensive experience in finance, banking, governance, technology, risk management, human resources, and corporate leadership. Under the leadership of Chairman and Independent/Non-Executive Director,\u00a0 K.M.M. Jabir, the Board consists of Neil Bogahalanda, Lalith Fernando, Muditha Welihinda and Shaheena Mohammed as Independent/Non-Executive Director. The Board also includes\u00a0 Prasanna Ranasinghe the Non-Independent Executive Director, who leads the team at Dearo Ventures Capital.\n\n\u201cOver the past four years, Dearo Venture Capital Ltd has emerged as a significant force within Sri Lanka\u2019s investment and financial services sector.Today, we serve more than 25,000 customers through a network of 25 branches island wide, supported by a dedicated workforce of over 350 professionals. Dearo Venture Capital Ltd has successfully built an asset base exceeding Rs.5 billion, reflecting the confidence and trust placed in the institution by investors and stakeholders across the country,\u201d noted Prasanna Ranasinghe.\n\nThe new Board is expected to provide strategic leadership and governance as Dearo Venture Capital Ltd expands its role as a catalyst for entrepreneurship, innovation, and sustainable economic development throughout Sri Lanka."
  },
