    "md5": "7393ff8440d35932e972698ca3198b31",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1894,
    "chunk_text": "Beyond technical architecture and corporate productivity, Chowhan is an outspoken proponent of inclusive leadership, viewing business enterprise as an instrument for broader societal development. Her perspective is deeply shaped by her six-year tenure serving on the board of the Latika Roy Foundation, an organisation in Dehradun, India, dedicated to supporting severely disabled children.\n\n\u201cFor me, inclusion is very broad. Inclusion means making sure that everybody has a seat at the table. Working with children with severe disabilities exposes you to a very different reality than what we are accustomed to in the corporate world and building empathy for that reality is essential.\u201d\n\nThis commitment to inclusion directly informs her outlook on corporate diversity and workforce modernisation. With female participation in Sri Lanka\u2019s formal labour force hovering around 30 percent, Chowhan pointed out that modern, flexible cloud technology can act as an equaliser, enabling women and working mothers to participate meaningfully in the economy.\n\nShe expressed an eagerness to engage directly with the local female executives and professionals during future engagements in Colombo to cultivate mentorship and leadership opportunities.\n\nLooking ahead, Chowhan expressed strong confidence in Sri Lanka\u2019s broader economic trajectory and its comprehensive national digital economy blueprint, which aims to achieve an annual economic growth rate of 5 percent, build a US $ 15 billion digital economy and skill 200,000 digital workers.\n\n\u201cSri Lanka is at a very good, pivotal time in the market,\u201d Chowhan observed.\n\n\u201cBetween the projected economic growth and the ambitious digital blueprint, the targets demonstrate immense promise. This is a very resilient market. We are here to support enterprises and help them serve their customers by unlocking the full power of technology.\u201d"
