    "chunk_size_bytes": 1352,
    "chunk_text": "Heavy rain triggers flash floods in Kandy\n\nColombo, Sep. 14 (Daily Mirror) - A sudden flood situation has been reported in a Divisional Secretariat Division in the Kandy District due to the heavy rainfall, Director of the Disaster Management Centre (DMC) Pradeep Kodippili said.\n\nHe said 25 persons from eight families have been affected by the flooding and have been temporarily relocated to the Bawwagama Vidyalaya in Nawalapitiya.\n\nRelief measures are currently being provided to the displaced families, he added.\n\nThe highest rainfall recorded over the past few hours was reported from Walallawita in the Kalutara District, where 119 mm of rain was recorded.\n\nRainfall ranging between 50 mm to 119 mm was also reported from Hanwella, Elpitiya, Neluwa, Dunhinna, Wathurawila and Naula, Kodippili said.\n\nHe said the DMC was prepared to respond to both the heavy rainfall affecting several areas and the dry weather conditions experienced in other parts of the country.\n\nThe public is urged to closely monitor weather alerts issued by the Department of Meteorology, while those living in hilly areas have been advised to remain vigilant for early signs of landslides.\n\nKodippili also urged the public to report any disaster-related situations to the DMC's emergency hotline 117.\n\nMirror Missions: El Ni\u00f1o in Sri Lanka, Can You Protect Your Community?"
