    "chunk_text": "Which is why so far, we have been successful as a new party which is more than two years old. As you can see, we don\u2019t have to transport people to our meetings. Instead, we work with our ground level network. There we promote entrepreneurship, creativity. We got youth and it\u2019s working organically.\n\nAnyone who accepts the basics of what we talk about on the concept of wealth creation for the nation we support. Whether we can form an alliance is a complexed situation to which I have to answer.\n\nA political force like NPP, whether they are open enough just for the sake of it. They can say that this is an entrepreneurial state or something that. Whether they believe in it, whether they have it in their DNA, in terms of implementation, whether they have the courage, and determination, those things matter.\n\nBut my biggest problem with the NPP is its, central ideology steming from the JVP. And the JVP isn\u2019t a party which believed in modern Economy. They still follow traditional beliefs. We need more than that. So, my submission and my proposition is that, when a political party does not have a progressive core philosophy, it is difficult to adapt to suit the modern world and the global competition. And realise the global economic challenges. So today, what is evident in their governance is that they are not susceptible, and ready. They are instead going in the most archaic manner that you can look at the world today.\n\nQIn your opinion, why is the government campaigning strongly for 22nd Amendment irrespective of the strong opposition from the BASL?"
