    "chunk_size_bytes": 1387,
    "chunk_text": "Moderated by corporate trainer Prassanna Pathmanathan, a panel featuring Gratiaen Prize-winning writer Dr. Ramya Jirasinghe, award-winning author and administrative officer Ciara Mandulee, and Sarasavi Bookshop Director Amendra Haputhanthri discussed how a simple thought can develop until it becomes a novel or a book.\n\nESU International Public Speaking Competition 2026 Winner Omar Hazari also spoke at the summit about pages, chapters and books, and how small steps shape our lives. He also spoke about how he was inspired to read through his mother\u2019s encouragement.\n\nFor Pick a Book, the next seven years could therefore be very different from the first seven. The movement is now asking individuals not only to pick up a book, but also to build the networks, habits and communities needed to make reading a national culture.\n\n\u201cThose are exactly the capacities that reading builds,\u201d Ragulan said, referring to thinking, imagination and deeper human connection.\n\n\u201cFor seven years, we asked people to pick a book, but now we are asking a nation to pick each other up -\u00a0 one reader, one club, one story at a time.\u201d\n\nBarista was the Title Sponsor, with Cinnamon Grand Colombo as Hospitality Partner, Daily FT as Print Media Partner and The Asian Review as Literary Partner. PickMe, GD, Zerostix, SLIQ, Softlogic GLOMARK and Vintage Ceylon also supported the event as partners."
