    "language": "en",
    "md5": "771cfd04c7328d07618f6f281b8c2c7c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1802,
    "chunk_text": "Located adjacent to the Aththanagalla Oya, the project was designed to withstand challenging environmental conditions, including potential flooding during heavy rainfall. Following a detailed assessment using historical data from the Irrigation Department, Hayleys Solar implemented an elevated solar mounting structure with increased clearance and safety margins, together with elevated inverter supports and customised cable routing systems to enhance the project\u2019s resilience.\n\nHayleys Fentons Ltd., Managing Director Hasith Prematillake said: \u201cThe Veyangoda project demonstrates our commitment to developing renewable energy solutions that respond to the realities of our environment. By integrating climate-resilient engineering with innovative land utilisation, we have created a solar installation that not only withstands challenging site conditions but also delivers greater value from the available land.\u201d\n\nThe 3 MW Hayleys Solar Veyangoda Ground-Mounted Solar Project, inaugurated as the first project under the 300 MW ground-mounted solar rollout\n\nThe project comprises 4,143.36 kWp of DC capacity and 3MW of AC capacity, featuring 640W bifacial solar panels, and is expected to generate approximately 6,351,770.88 kWh of clean electricity annually - enough to meet the annual electricity needs of around 2,700 average Sri Lankan households\u00b9 while avoiding approximately 4,339.53 tonnes of CO2 emissions each year.\n\nWith an average clearance of approximately 2.7 metres above ground level, the elevated structure also enables productive use of the land beneath the solar panels. As part of an agrivoltaic initiative, the space will support the cultivation of vegetables such as Scotch bonnet pepper and brinjal, enabling agricultural production alongside renewable energy generation."
  },
