    "chunk_size_bytes": 1739,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cGem Sri Lanka 2027\u201d woos Thailand buyers\n\nSri Lankan exports to Thailand more than doubled in 2025 to over $ 90 m\u00a0with precious and semi-precious stones accounting for almost 70%\n\nThe \u201cGem Sri Lanka 2027\u201d was unveiled in Bangkok on 6 September, bringing together key stakeholders to promote Sri Lanka\u2019s gem and jewellery industry ahead of its fourth edition in January 2027.\n\nThe launch was organised by the Ceylon Gem and Jewellery Traders Association (CGJTA).\n\nThe event was attended by the Chief Guest, Industry and Entrepreneurship Development Minister Sunil Handunnetti, who delivered the keynote address.\n\nHe highlighted the importance of value addition, innovation and international collaboration in strengthening Sri Lanka\u2019s gem and jewellery industry, as well as the significant opportunities for Sri Lanka\u2013Thailand cooperation in gem cutting, processing, jewellery manufacturing, design, technology and international marketing.\n\nThe Minister further noted that Sri Lanka\u2019s precious stones and centuries-old craftsmanship, together with Thailand\u2019s globally recognised expertise in gemstone processing, jewellery manufacturing, design and international marketing, provided a strong foundation for deeper industry partnerships. He emphasised the potential to move beyond traditional trading relationships and strengthen cooperation through skills development, technology transfer, research and innovation.\n\nAmbassador of Sri Lanka to Thailand, Wijayanthi Edirisinghe, participated in a panel discussion on \u201cStrengthening Sri Lanka\u2019s Gem and Jewellery Industry and Expanding Its Global Presence\u201d, alongside National Gem and Jewellery Authority (NGJA) Chairman Dr. S. P. Chaminda, and other industry leaders."
  },
