    "md5": "acfa50599f78c0876ebab516226507dd",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1977,
    "chunk_text": "Euro Motors revamps spare parts showroom\n\nManagement and representatives of Euro Motors cut the ribbon to reopen the showroom\n\nEuro Motors has recently relaunched its dedicated Spare Parts Showroom, located at Sri Saddharma Mawatha, Colombo-10, offering customers access to a range of genuine spare parts for vehicles across its portfolio of brandsfor both passenger vehicles and trucks & busses, including Jetour, Dongfeng, JAC, Bonluck, Ankai and Joylong.\n\nThe newly revamped showroom is designed to make sourcing the right spare parts easier and more convenient for individual vehicle owners, corporate customers, fleet operators and insurance companies seeking reliable solutions for accident repairs.\n\nBringing a wide selection of genuine spare parts together under one roof, the showroom provides customers with a single, accessible destination for their vehicle maintenance and repair requirements.\n\nAdding to the convenience is an easy ordering and delivery service. Customers who are unable to visit the showroom can contact the Spare Parts Showroom directly to enquire about and order the parts they require.\n\nThe relaunch also introduces a range of attractive bundle offers, giving customers added value when purchasing spare parts for their vehicles. These offers are designed to make genuine replacement parts more accessible while providing customers with a convenient and cost-effective way to address their vehicle maintenance requirements.\n\nFor owners of high-value vehicles, the choice of Genuine spare parts can have a significant impact on long-term vehicle performance and durability. Genuine spare parts are specifically designed to meet the specifications of the respective vehicle, helping ensure compatibility, reliability and consistent performance. This is particularly important for vehicles within their warranty period, and thereafterwhere using the appropriate genuine components can help protect the vehicle and the investment made by the owner."
  },
