    "chunk_size_bytes": 1966,
    "chunk_text": "Maliban\u2019s HumanTill wins Crystal at MAD STARS 2026\n\nMaliban\u2019s HumaniTill campaign has achieved international recognition by winning a Crystal Award at MAD STARS 2026 under the Brand Experience & Activation Stars | Culture & Context category, marking another milestone for Sri Lankan creativity on the global stage.\n\nThe recognition celebrates a campaign that transformed a simple yet powerful idea rooted in empathy into a meaningful brand experience, demonstrating how creativity can go beyond communication to create positive social impact.\n\nMAD STARS, one of Asia\u2019s recognised global creative platforms, celebrates innovative ideas across advertising, marketing, and brand experiences. The awards recognise work that demonstrates creativity, cultural relevance, strategic thinking, and the ability to create meaningful connections with audiences, positioning winning work among the region\u2019s most impactful creative initiatives.\n\nThe HumaniTill campaign was introduced under the Maliban Jeewithaloka Programme, with the aim of becoming a source of strength and hope for Sri Lankans facing life-changing challenges. The initiative was carried out in collaboration with the Meththa Foundation, a humanitarian organisation that has been supporting people with disabilities for over three decades by providing customised artificial limbs and helping them regain mobility, independence, and confidence.\n\nUnlike a conventional donation box, HumaniTill was designed as a life-sized human figure featuring a transparent arm and leg, symbolising individuals who have lost limbs due to accidents or illness. The installation served as a powerful reminder of the importance of giving and the possibility of providing someone with a second chance at life.\n\nThe Crystal Award at MAD STARS 2026 further reinforces the impact of HumaniTill, recognising the campaign\u2019s ability to combine purpose, creativity, and community participation into a powerful brand experience."
