    "md5": "83481295079542a74f5378abe581e913",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2012,
    "chunk_text": "Prime Group\u2019s The Colombo Border tops off all three towers\n\nPrime Lands Residencies PLC, the condominium development arm of Prime Group, has announced the completion of the superstructures of all three towers at The Colombo Border, marking a key construction milestone.\n\nThe breakthrough follows the prior topping out of Tower Cosmos and confirms that the entire project has moved through its most complex construction phase, ahead of the original schedule.\n\nThe Colombo Border by Prime Lands Residencies PLC is a landmark residential development that redefines urban living at the gateway to Colombo.\n\nSituated in the emerging residential hub of Peliyagoda, the project has been designed to offer a complete lifestyle experience that combines convenience, connectivity, recreation, sustainability, and community living.\n\nSpread across approximately 6.5 acres ofPrime real estate, The Colombo Border comprises three residential towers, Brielle, Cosmos, and Amaa, offering thoughtfully designed two- and three-bedroom residences and few four-bedroom penthouses. Approximately 5 acres of the development have been dedicated to landscaped gardens, leisure spaces, recreational amenities, and open green areas, creating a vibrant and enriching environment where residents may enjoy a balanced lifestyle surrounded by comfort, convenience, and nature.\n\nThe completion of the superstructure of all three towers marks a major milestone for The Colombo Border, bringing one of Colombo\u2019s largest integrated residential developments significantly closer to completion with handover set to commence from 2027 mid onwards.\n\nThe pace at which the project has advanced reflects the strength of the construction planning behind it, as well as the coordinated execution of two specialized engineering teams working in parallel across the site. Prime Construction (Pvt) Ltd, the Group\u2019s in-house construction arm, leads the construction of two towers, while Sanken Lanka (Pvt) Ltd leads the construction of the other tower."
  },
