    "chunk_index": 3,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "24468c13617ffb358195cf40f5177c12",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 740,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka also sought membership of the New Development Bank. For a country recovering from sovereign default and requiring substantial infrastructure investment, expanding access to long-term development finance should be a strategic priority. This is not a choice between the IMF, World Bank, Asian Development Bank or BRICS institutions.\n\nColombo must ask one simple question. Why are we not in the room and what are we doing to make certain that when the door opens again, Sri Lanka walks through it?\n\nOthers saw the opportunity, lobbied and moved ahead. Sri Lanka cannot afford to remain a spectator. The Global South is building new economic bridges. We should be helping to build them not standing on the shore watching others cross."
