    "md5": "eee8da7adf47eaf256a9af58caa768d0",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1809,
    "chunk_text": "Digital Mobility Solutions Lanka appoints Priyanthini McNair to board\n\nDigital Mobility Solutions Lanka PLC (DMSL), the company behind Sri Lanka\u2019s homegrown digital platform PickMe, has appointed seasoned international banking professional Priyanthini McNair as an Independent Non-Executive Director, strengthening its board with deep expertise in corporate banking, finance, governance, risk and strategic growth.\n\nMcNair brings more than 25 years of international experience across the UK, Hong Kong, the MENAT region, India and Singapore and is the founder of APG Management Consulting.\n\nMore recently, she served as Global Co-Head of Corporate Coverage and Senior Managing Director at Emirates NBD Group, where she led international corporate banking, overseeing a multi-billion-dollar portfolio and global sector coverage across seven countries.\n\n\u201cWe are pleased to welcome Priyanthini McNair to the board. Her extensive banking experience and international exposure bring valuable expertise as we enter our next phase of development,\u201d said DMSL founder and CEO Jiffry Zulfer.\n\n\u201cAs a publicly listed company, her background will be particularly relevant as we expand our existing product verticals and explore new adjacent opportunities to drive our growth.\u00a0 As an Independent Non-Executive Director, her perspective will also contribute to strengthening our governance framework and building greater confidence among the investors and other stakeholders.\u201d\n\nPrior to Emirates NBD, McNair spent over two decades with HSBC in senior leadership roles. These included Regional Head of Coverage for Commercial Banking across MENAT, based in Dubai, UK Head of Leveraged Corporates in London and Global Head of Business Development and Chief of Staff for Large Corporates across the UK and Hong Kong."
  },
