    "chunk_size_bytes": 1530,
    "chunk_text": "Sept. 25-Oct. 1 declared National Children\u2019s Day Week\n\nColombo, Sep. 15 (Daily Mirror) - The Cabinet has approved the declaration of September 25 to October 1, 2026 as \u2018National Children\u2019s Day Week - 2026\u2019 to raise public awareness of children\u2019s rights and strengthen community participation in child protection.\n\nChildren\u2019s Day is celebrated annually in Sri Lanka on October 1, with the aim of promoting awareness of children\u2019s rights, education, health and well-being.\n\nThe Government has observed that the challenges faced by children have expanded beyond traditional child protection concerns, with children increasingly exposed to risks associated with the Internet and digital technology, psychological and social pressures, neglect and various social and economic challenges.\n\nThe Government has also identified the need to improve awareness of children\u2019s rights and protection among parents, teachers, government officials, service providers and members of the public who regularly interact with children.\n\nAccordingly, the National Children\u2019s Day Week will be conducted alongside the National Children\u2019s Day celebration programme, with special programmes planned to increase public awareness, strengthen social sensitivity towards children and encourage greater community involvement in child protection.\n\nThe proposal to declare September 25 to October 1 as \u2018National Children\u2019s Day Week - 2026\u2019 was submitted by the Minister of Women and Child Affairs and subsequently approved by the Cabinet."
