    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "0071b7eb87c1b207ddc2ef2a1b056372",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1851,
    "chunk_text": "Why is system change  so tricky and elusive?\n\nCorruption in the public sector is coupled with the lethargy from\u00a0 top to bottom of the rank and file\n\nAs if justifying the delay in the implementation of government\u2019s promises, Deputy Minister of Transport and Highways Dr. Prasanna Gunasena has stated that although his party, the National People\u2019s Power (NPP) has gained power of government, it has not gained the state power in its entirety.\n\nHe apparently means that state machinery, mainly the officialdom,\u00a0 is not under the full control of the party and hence, things are not moving at the pace the party and the government desire.\n\nThis is the standpoint of the NPP leaders since they took the reins two years ago. We remember that two ministers of the NPP government in December, 2024\u00a0 expressed their frustration over the lack of cooperation on the part of a section of the officialdom in their efforts to make changes in the existing system.\n\nAgriculture Minister K.D. Lalkantha had accused bureaucrats for obstructing the Government from taking the country forward. A controversial figure, Lal Kantha warned: \u201cThe next tsunami will happen against the corrupt bureaucracy of this country.\u201d Minister of Industries Sunil Handunnetti also during an event said that the \u201cstate officials, who have got used to work according to the corrupt policies and practices of former governments,\u00a0 are not prepared yet to get rid of those old practices.\u201d\n\nDuring a discussion with the heads of the Department of Immigration and Emigration, Sri Lanka Customs, and Airport and Aviation Services, President Anura Kumara Dissanayake also highlighted early last year the need to eliminate negative perceptions surrounding Sri Lanka Customs and underscored the urgency of implementing strict disciplinary and legal action to restore public confidence."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-09-16-dailymirrorlk-359fe019",
    "num": "dailymirrorlk-359fe019",
