    "md5": "f8ff0577f7ba5e2a0818b316d3e03f57",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1711,
    "chunk_text": "Billing in Sri Lankan rupees gives local businesses greater predictability and control over AI expenditure, while local infrastructure and engineering support provide a closer-to-home option for organisations looking to build and operate AI applications.\n\nRoar AI is not a standalone AI application or chatbot. It acts as an infrastructure layer that allows developers to connect AI models to their own products, platforms and workflows. This gives teams the flexibility to experiment with different models, optimise for performance and cost, and scale their AI capabilities through one locally supported platform.\n\nThe launch reflects Roar Global\u2019s broader evolution from a digital media and platform consultancy into a venture-building group operating across AI, technology platforms and the creator economy. The Group has made significant investments in AI-led innovation, with its teams already processing more than 10 billion AI tokens across the products, applications and workflows it has built.\n\nRoar AI also represents a wider commitment to strengthening Sri Lanka\u2019s participation in the global AI economy. By making advanced AI infrastructure easier to access locally, Roar aims to help developers, entrepreneurs and enterprises move beyond experimenting with individual AI tools and towards building scalable products and businesses with AI at their core.\n\n\u201cWe don\u2019t want Sri Lanka to simply be a market that consumes AI products built elsewhere,\u201d Mustafa added. \u201cWe want Sri Lankan developers and businesses to have the infrastructure to build those products here and take them to the world.\u201d\n\nRoar AI is currently being introduced to selected builders and early adopters in Sri Lanka."
