    "md5": "c2de20f5eef76d7390ee1f54c27bb66a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1633,
    "chunk_text": "FCCISL hails National Business Facilitation Centre\n\nSays Cabinet approval marks landmark step towards regional and national business recovery, expansion and integration into economic value chains\n\nThe Federation of Chambers of Commerce and Industry of Sri Lanka (FCCISL), under the leadership of President Dr. Rohitha Silva, together with State Affairs Committee Chairman and Director Ruwan De Silva, and the Board of Directors, has welcomed Cabinet approval to establish the National Business Facilitation Centre (NBFC).\n\nIn a statement FCCISL expressed its sincere gratitude to President Anura Kumara Dissanayake, the Cabinet of Ministers, Members of Parliament, the Presidential Secretariat, public officials and stakeholders supporting this initiative.\n\nSpecial appreciation is extended to Senior Additional Secretary to the President Seevali Arukgoda, and his team for consulting the business community on longstanding issues, experiences and practical proposals.\n\nFCCISL highlights the cumulative strain on enterprises from the Easter Sunday attacks, COVID-19 and its aftermath, the sudden economic collapse, the economic crisis, continuing recessionary pressures on businesses, Cyclone Ditwah, global conflicts, trade wars, geopolitical rivalries and climate change impacts.\n\nThese successive shocks have weakened financial capacity and human capital, constrained investment in machinery and equipment, delayed digitalisation and AI adoption, and disrupted manufacturing and production. They have also affected service reliability, quality standards and businesses\u2019 ability to fulfil contractual and performance obligations."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-09-17-dailyftlk-bbc49d9f",
    "num": "dailyftlk-bbc49d9f",
