    "chunk_size_bytes": 1606,
    "chunk_text": "The participants also explored how technological innovation and artificial intelligence could support reserve management through enhanced investment decision-making, market intelligence, portfolio optimisation and risk management.\n\nThe keynote address was delivered by Central Bank Governor Dr. Nandalal Weerasinghe, on \u2018Challenges in Building Foreign Reserves Amidst Geopolitical Uncertainties\u2019.\n\nDrawing on Sri Lanka\u2019s experience during the 2022 economic crisis, Dr. Weerasinghe highlighted the critical role of international reserves as a first line of defence against external shocks, providing countries with valuable time and policy space during periods of heightened vulnerability.\n\nDr. Weerasinghe further noted that geopolitical developments have become an increasingly important consideration for reserve managers, with fragmentation, sanctions, trade tensions and disruptions to global financial markets influencing investment, liquidity and portfolio management decisions.\n\nA Special Guest Address was delivered by AIIB Treasurer Domenico Nardelli, who shared his perspectives on the evolving international financial landscape and its implications for reserve and asset management.\n\nOver the two days, expert presentations and panel discussions facilitated in-depth dialogue on emerging developments and strategic issues in reserve management. The conference provided an opportunity to draw on diverse international experiences, share lessons and innovative approaches and strengthen professional networks among central banks, international financial institutions and market participants."
