    "md5": "a1327b7058d6652b4ba9105089bf2f42",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1906,
    "chunk_text": "Janashakthi Finance profit plunges 84% as auditors warn Rs.270mn hole may run deeper\n\nAudited FY26 profit at Rs.64.7mn, against Rs.402.7mn in interim accounts\n\nFurther adjustments to profit, assets and EPS cannot yet be quantified\n\nJanashakthi Finance PLC\u2019s audited profit for the year ended March 2026 came in 84 percent below the figure it had earlier disclosed to the market, after its auditors qualified the accounts over an unreconciled Rs.270.5 million balance, which the company is yet to account for, a filing with the Colombo Stock Exchange (CSE) showed.\n\nThe company further warned that the hit to its financials may deepen. Since the auditors were unable to determine whether further adjustments would be necessary, \u201cany additional cumulative impact on profit or loss, net assets, total assets, total income, earnings per share or any other financial statement item cannot presently be reliably quantified\u201d, according to the filing.\n\nThe finance company, formerly Orient Finance PLC, reported an audited profit of Rs.64.7 million, against the Rs.402.7 million shown in its interim accounts, a revision which cuts earnings per share to about Rs.0.31, from an implied Rs.1.91.\n\nThe qualification centres on a debit balance of Rs.270,542,779 carried under other assets, against which the company made a full provision, noting that \u201cthe reconciliation process was not completed prior to the approval of the financial statements\u201d.\n\nKPMG, the company\u2019s external auditors, \u201cwere unable to obtain sufficient appropriate audit evidence regarding the nature, accuracy, classification and recoverability\u201d of the balance, nor could they verify whether the provision itself was adequate.\n\nThe provision alone is equivalent to 48 percent of the pre-tax profit reported in the interim accounts and 7 percent of equity. However, it accounts for only part of the Rs.338 million decline in profit."
  },
