    "chunk_text": "He said euthanasia would only be permitted where a government veterinary surgeon confirms that an animal is infected with rabies and considers it necessary to prevent a danger to the public. The procedure must be carried out by the government veterinary surgeon or a person authorised by the veterinarian.\n\n\u201cRabies control is now governed by scientific, humane and veterinary medical protocols,\u201d he said.\n\nThe new legislation also introduces mandatory annual rabies vaccination and registration of dogs, while placing greater responsibility on local authorities and dog owners for rabies prevention and dog population management.\n\nThe Bill also provides for the repeal of the existing Rabies Ordinance and Dog Registration Ordinance, replacing the previous legal framework with a comprehensive system covering rabies elimination, vaccination, dog registration, sterilisation and regulation of commercial breeding.\n\nDr. Nanayakkara said that the new framework means that suspicion of rabies alone should not be treated as grounds for the arbitrary killing of an animal.\n\n\u201cNo one has the legal authority to arbitrarily kill, have the police shoot, or inflict cruelty upon animals based on a suspicion of rabies,\u201d he said."
