    "date_str": "2026-09-17",
    "description": "The Opposition:  NPP\u2019s greatest asset",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/opinion/The-Opposition-NPPs-greatest-asset/172-350506",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1789625824.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-09-17-dailymirrorlk-15e9b722-0002",
    "chunk_index": 2,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "16583d834f41d5d282bf30472083dc89",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1822,
    "chunk_text": "This marks a glaring contradiction: the initial investigations into the Airbus scandal were launched in 2015 under UNP-led government before being shelved. Now that the current administration has revived the case and executed the arrest, the UNP ironically decries it as political victimisation.\n\nWeerasinghe alleged that former Minister Chandrasena had defrauded farmers by mixing lake silt with tire ash to sell as organic fertiliser. Kuttiarachchi similarly pinned the blame for the infamous Gotabaya-era organic fertiliser crisis directly on Mahindananda Aluthgamage\u2014conveniently ignoring the fact that they themselves were part of the very same government when those policies were enacted.\n\nThe most shocking moment occurred during MP Archchuna\u2019s speech, where he openly identified himself as a \u201cTiger\u201d closely linked to the Tamil diaspora while launching a fierce attack on the government. Shockingly, southern nationalist leaders like Weerawansa and Gammanpila seemed to be enjoying the speech while the crowd cheered along. At one point, before addressing Tamil politics, Weerawansa went as far as expressing personal regret to Archchuna.\n\nHad a Tamil politician stood up at any other party rally and proclaimed \u201cI am a Tiger,\u201d the reaction from these SLPP leaders would have been radically hostile. By coddling a self-proclaimed Tiger at their rally simply to attack the current government, these leaders have proven that their long-standing brand of fiery patriotism was nothing more than a political hoax.\n\nFurthermore, this shows that if Mahinda Rajapaksa genuinely cared about resolving the ethnic problem when he was at the peak of his power,\u00a0 he could have succeeded, as his supporters who cheered a man who publicly claimed to be a \u201cTiger\u201d wouldn\u2019t have opposed any of the Tamil demands."
  },
