    "md5": "39d4603c2ed0e2f44f5895048402f083",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1018,
    "chunk_text": "SLPP member Renuka Perera arrested\n\nColombo, September 17 (Daily Mirror) - The Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery or Corruption (CIABOC) has arrested Sri Lanka Podujana Peramuna (SLPP) member and former National Transport Commission (NTC) Chairman Renuka Perera over corruption allegations involving bus permits for the Southern Expressway.\n\nAccording to the CIABOC, the investigation centres on accusations that Perera had illegally issued 56 Southern Expressway passenger service permits to third parties without following statutory procedures outlined in the National Transport Commission Act No. 37 of 1991.\n\nThe former chairman is also accused of bypassing recommendations set by a Cabinet decision on September 19, 2014, and failing to collect mandatory annual license fees, resulting in significant unlawful financial losses to the State while conferring improper advantages to private operators.\n\nThe suspect will be produced before the Colombo Chief Magistrate\u2019s Court for further proceedings."
  },
