    "md5": "4b9f3eb4d000a2234b31682d96eadbdf",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 976,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka, Thailand expedite visa-free travel talks\n\nThailand, September 17 (Daily Mirror) - Sri Lanka and Thailand have agreed to further strengthen bilateral relations, with both sides discussing steps to expedite arrangements for visa exemption for holders of ordinary passports.\n\nThe agreement was reached during a meeting between Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism Minister Vijitha Herath and Thailand\u2019s Acting Minister of Foreign Affairs Sarun Charoensuwan in Bangkok.\n\nThe proposed visa exemption is expected to facilitate travel, boost tourism and promote greater people-to-people exchanges between the two countries.\n\nThe two ministers also discussed expanding cooperation in trade, investment, tourism, labour mobility, education, maritime security and cultural exchanges.\n\nThe meeting reaffirmed the commitment of both countries to deepen Sri Lanka-Thailand relations and advance practical areas of cooperation for the mutual benefit of their people."
  },
