    "md5": "f2f45cd75a97565f0d6412b4e814051d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1846,
    "chunk_text": "A nation powered by nature: Sri Lanka\u2019s first battery energy storage system commissioning turns new chapter in energy journey\n\nAccording to the Sri Lanka Sustainable Energy Authority, the country\u2019s renewable energy potential exceeds 13,000 MW\n\nBy investing early, Sri Lanka positions itself as a climate-resilient island nation, setting an example for other Asian countries\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s dependence on imported fuels exposes the nation to international price volatility and foreign exchange pressures\n\nGalilee BESS (Pvt) Ltd, a subsidiary of WKV Hydro Technics (Pvt) Ltd and wholly owned by Khen Energy Ltd, has successfully completed the commissioning process mandated by the National System Operator (NSO). This milestone culminated in the commissioning of Sri Lanka\u2019s first-ever 10MW/40MWh Battery Energy Storage System (BESS) in Galle on 10th September 2026.\n\nThe achievement was made possible not only through corporate commitment and technical expertise, but also through the Government\u2019s decisive leadership and expedited facilitation of the BESS initiative within a remarkably short period of time.\n\nBESS is an integrated system that stabilises power grids, supports renewable energy, and strengthens economic resilience. For Sri Lanka, the commissioning of its first BESS in Galle is both a technological milestone and a strategic policy achievement a catalyst for industrial ecosystems and a foundation for regional leadership in the global sustainable energy transition.\n\nThis landmark achievement inaugurates a new chapter in Sri Lanka\u2019s energy journey, one where storage technology transforms the country\u2019s abundant renewable resources into dependable, dispatchable power. This partnership between the public and private sectors marks a historic breakthrough, advancing resilience, sustainability, and national progress."
  },
