    "md5": "27d755238f4fea9d06b68fffe9d9daf1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1655,
    "chunk_text": "The vision must extend beyond national borders. South Asia is one of the fastest-growing energy markets in the world, with energy demand projected to grow at 6% annually, while fossil fuels still account for 70% of the region\u2019s primary energy supply (International Energy Agency, 2025). This imbalance underscores the urgency of scalable renewable solutions.\n\nToday, roughly 8\u201310 Asian countries have meaningful grid-scale BESS deployment: China, India, Japan, South Korea, Australia, Philippines, Vietnam, Taiwan, and now Sri Lanka, with newer entrants emerging. The broader ASEAN bloc is still building out regulatory frameworks to catch up.\n\nIndeed, Sri Lanka can become a role model for Asia. Our nation, though small in size, can show how intelligent planning, early investment in storage, and the harnessing of natural assets deliver resilience, prosperity, and leadership. Larger economies across Asia many of which face similar challenges of fuel dependence, climate vulnerability, and rising demand can look to Sri Lanka\u2019s example as proof that clean energy can be reliable, affordable, and scalable.\n\nEnergy transition is not only a matter for governments and institutions it is a matter for every citizen.\u00a0 People must understand that when we invest in BESS, we are investing in cleaner air, more reliable electricity, reduced fuel imports, and a stronger economy.\n\nThis is a generational opportunity. For our youth, it means new jobs, new industries, and new skills. For our communities, it means resilience against climate shocks and greater reliability in daily life. For our nation, it means independence, prosperity, and leadership."
