    "md5": "d100b73bfa51c7c29d82a3d1279acae6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1594,
    "chunk_text": "This is a generational opportunity. For our youth, it means new jobs, new industries, and new skills. For our communities, it means resilience against climate shocks and greater reliability in daily life. For our nation, it means independence, prosperity, and leadership.\n\nThe sun that warms our homes, the wind that sweeps across our fields, and the rivers that flow through our land are not abstractions they are gifts of nature entrusted to our stewardship. With storage, technology, investment, and leadership, these gifts can be transformed into dependable power, stronger economic performance, and enduring prosperity.\n\nThis is a moment that calls for national vision and coordinated regional action. What Sri Lanka has long awaited the storage, the technology, the investment, and the leadership are now within our grasp, ready to be harnessed not only for our nation, but for South Asia and Asia at large.\u00a0 That future has already begun.\u00a0 The commissioning of Sri Lanka\u2019s first Battery Energy Storage System in Galle stands as living proof that this vision is no longer aspirational it is already unfolding.\n\nThe energy challenge of tomorrow calls for action today. Let us build the capacity that empowers Sri Lanka to inspire Asia and brighten a cleaner, more resilient future for generations to come.\n\n(The writer is Director Strategic Development WKV Group, Director Khen Energy, Senior Fellow South Asia Foresight Network, Vice\n\nPresident OPA, Immediate Past President Association of Retired Flag Rank Officers, Formerly Commander Sri Lanka Air Force, Ambassador to Afghanistan)"
