    "chunk_text": "\u201cSri Lanka is experiencing heavy weather in Geneva as a result of govt.\u2019s broken promises\u201d  Prof. G. L Peiris, Former Minister\n\n\u201cLocking people up every day and having a media blitzkrieg about the number of people being taken into custody is alright if it\u2019s being done according to due process\u201d G.L. Peiris, Former Minister\n\nThe 22A among other deleterious consequences will discourage serious foreign investors from coming into the country\n\nNobody has seen any draft of legislation to establish a Truth and Reconciliation Commission\n\nThe report says that there should be significant improvement of the independent capacity of the OMP\n\nA significant conclusion set out in the report is that the trust in domestic accountability mechanisms remains low\n\nThe 63rd session of the United Nations Human Rights Council (UNHRC) is currently underway in Geneva. The UN High Commissioner for Human Rights Volker T\u00fcrk released a comprehensive report on Sri Lanka, urging robust accountability, institutional reforms and a moratorium on the Prevention of Terrorism Act.As an experienced politician who served various portfolios as a foreign minister and minister of external affairs and having represented Sri Lanka on various international platforms, Prof. G. L. Peiris spoke to the Daily Mirror regarding his observations on the High Commissioner\u2019s report. He raised concerns regarding the way the incumbent government is handling the country\u2019s foreign policy while highlighting repercussions of the inability to deliver its promises made to international organisations such as the United Nations. Excerpts:\n\nQ What are your thoughts regarding United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights Volker T\u00fcrk\u2019s report on Sri Lanka?"
