    "chunk_text": "Q Successive governments have held numerous discussions regarding the Truth and Reconciliation Commission especially during election periods. This government also promised to establish this Commission. What are your comments?\n\nThere are stringent criticisms relating to the Office on Missing Persons. The report says that there should be significant improvement of the independent capacity of the OMP. That they should have adequate investigative powers in order to fulfill their mandate credibly. A significant conclusion set out in the report is that the trust in domestic accountability mechanisms remains low.\n\nQ We have had several domestic processes to ensure justice for communities affected by the war. But many of them have been stalled or lacks tangible progress. What do you have to say?\n\nIt is an age-old problem and it\u2019s not something that can be fixed overnight. There\u2019s no need to reinvent the wheel. There\u2019s so much material that is available. There have been so many commissions, committees and so on which have done valuable work. What is required is a fresh evaluation of the abundant material that is already in existence. Not to add one more leaf to the thicket, but to make a comprehensive appraisal of the already existing material. That\u2019s what the government promised to do. But nothing has happened.\n\nQThe government is determined to pass the controversial 22nd Amendment. But you have been quite critical about this move."
