    "chunk_size_bytes": 1529,
    "chunk_text": "Q The High Commissioner\u2019s report also refers to arbitrary arrests, torture, detentions and custodial deaths which portray a negative picture about the country\u2019s human rights situation. What are your comments?\n\nQ There was no Sri Lankan delegation at the recently concluded BRICS Summit held in India. Isn\u2019t it an opportunity that we missed?\n\nBRICS is an institution which would have been of enormous value to Sri Lanka. The main theme in the recently concluded BRICS sessions was \u2018resistance of unilateralism.\u2019 During their meeting they passed a resolution to say that unilateral tariffs constitute a violation of World Trade Organisation (WTO) rules. They said that BRICS must collectively act against it. Then they referred to emerging markets in the global south and developing countries and it was very much the focus of attention. There was a very powerful participation of countries such as China, India, Russia, South Africa, Brazil and Iran. BRICS is going to establish a New Development Bank to provide resources for emerging countries. This would be on parallel with the IMF, the World Bank, Asian Development Bank and so on. We desperately need those resources. We cannot rely on one source. We need a multiplicity of resources. But Sri Lanka was not represented at all. We didn\u2019t send anybody there. This is inexcusable and we are letting these valuable opportunities slip through our fingers.\n\nQ What are your thoughts regarding the way the country\u2019s foreign policy is being handled by this government?"
