    "chunk_text": "Q The incumbent government is carrying out investigations into financial crimes committed during previous regimes and some of them involve high profile figures. But the opposition has been urging the release of some of these individuals currently detained or behind bars. What are your comments?\n\nQ Sri Lanka\u2019s peace process failed as mentioned in your book. Today we see many narratives by LTTE sympathisers to gain sympathy from the international community. How do you see these attempts?\n\nThat is to be expected. The war ended in 2009 but the diaspora is active in all these countries. Many of these countries have extended their bans on LTTE. The diaspora is doing whatever they are naturally expected to do. But it is not proper for a government to be controlled or for their decisions to be dictated by the diaspora. Diaspora has abundant funds and with that comes influence. But the government must act in the interests of its own people. The diaspora shouldn\u2019t be the determining or defining factor.\n\nQ How optimistic are you that the Opposition has a chance to field a winning candidate in the next election?"
