    "language": "en",
    "md5": "fd59cdbc770fd1449a81a6c3a60fd805",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1925,
    "chunk_text": "He said the changing environment meant both young people entering employment and established professionals needed to continuously reassess their capabilities and understand where new opportunities were emerging.\n\nNextTier seeks to address this gap by exposing participants to areas including AI, analytics, FinTech, project management, recruitment, leadership, management and macroeconomics.\n\nFor the second consecutive year, the program will select 35 participants for structured engagement with 12 local and international WIM Global mentors, providing access to their experience and perspectives in preparation for greater leadership responsibilities.\n\nWomen MSME Awards 2026 judging panel Chair Prashantha Mahadevan said the awards would recognise entrepreneurs not only for business success, but also for the wider economic and social impact they create.\n\n\u201cThe Women MSME Awards 2026 are not simply about recognising businesses that are successful. They are about recognising women who are going beyond running a business,\u201d he said.\n\n\u201cWe are looking at women who are creating employment, generating economic value, driving innovation and making a positive social impact.\u201d\n\nMahadevan said the judging process would take into account the individual journeys of entrepreneurs, recognising that businesses develop under different circumstances and with varying levels of resources.\n\n\u201cEvery business has a story, and every entrepreneur has faced different challenges,\u201d he said.\n\nEmployment creation would be an important consideration in the evaluation process, he added.\n\n\u201cWhen a woman entrepreneur creates jobs, she is not only growing her own business. She is creating opportunities for other people and supporting families and communities.\u201d\n\nInnovation would also be considered broadly, ranging from products and services to technology adoption and new approaches to solving business and social challenges."
  },
