    "chunk_size_bytes": 1828,
    "chunk_text": "Govt. aims to increase Samurdhi loans to Rs.70 bn next year\n\nColombo, Septemeber 18 (Daily Mirror) - The Government plans to increase the value of loans provided through the Samurdhi banking system from around Rs.60 billion last year to Rs.70 billion next year, Minister of Rural Development, Social Security and Community Empowerment Dr. Upali Pannila said.\n\nAddressing an awareness programme for Samurdhi officials in Matara and Hambantota, Minister Pannila said the Samurdhi banking system should be used as an important mechanism to economically empower low-income communities.\n\nHe said approximately Rs.60 billion in loans had been disbursed to the public through the Samurdhi banking system last year, while the Government expects to increase the amount to Rs.70 billion next year.\n\nThe Minister said the Government's objective was to eradicate poverty within the current generation by transforming people from dependency into economically and socially empowered citizens.\n\nHe said the Samurdhi Development Department must be comprehensively restructured to respond to current social, political and economic conditions and public aspirations.\n\nThe Government has entrusted the department with empowering 1.2 million \u2018Aswesuma\u2019 beneficiary families by 2029 through a range of programmes.\n\nThese include the \u2018Savibala\u2019 loan scheme, micro-credit facilities for small businesses, vocational training loans for youth, self-employment training and equipment, and livelihood development programmes.\n\nThe Minister was addressing the \u2018Praja Saviyata New Balayak\u2019 programme, which is being conducted islandwide to strengthen and streamline Samurdhi empowerment initiatives.\n\nThe Matara and Hambantota district programme was held on September 16 at the Rabindranath Tagore Memorial Auditorium of the University of Ruhuna."
  },
