    "chunk_text": "The President said the IMF-supported programme had provided an important foundation for restoring stability following Sri Lanka\u2019s worst economic crisis in decades. He added that the improved economic position had strengthened the country\u2019s ability to absorb the fallout from Cyclone Ditwah and the conflict in the Middle East.\n\nHowever, the latest growth data also showed an uneven rebound, with stronger performances in some productive sectors yet to translate fully into broad improvements in household welfare.\n\nThe President reiterated that safeguarding economic stability remained a central priority, citing the government\u2019s tax revenue performance over the past two years.\n\nThe IMF delegation also reviewed progress in implementing the country\u2019s social welfare benefit programme, a key commitment under the EFF, while the impact of higher energy costs linked to the Middle East conflict was also discussed.\n\nCentral Bank Governor Dr. P. Nandalal Weerasinghe, Finance Ministry Secretary Dr. Harshana Suriyapperuma and Senior Economic Advisor to the President Duminda Hulangamuwa were among the Sri Lankan officials who participated in the discussions."
