    "chunk_size_bytes": 771,
    "chunk_text": "He said there had been a significant change in the way investigations were conducted, noting that powerful individuals could no longer expect investigators to visit their homes to obtain statements simply because of their positions.\n\nHe said legal notices could be issued under Section 106 to summon individuals who were in the country, while those who had fled overseas could be pursued through international mechanisms, including Interpol Red Notices, to secure their return to Sri Lanka.\n\nThe Deputy Minister said 74 individuals allegedly linked to international drug networks had already been apprehended and brought back to Sri Lanka, describing this as an example of the authorities\u2019 efforts to ensure that suspects could not evade justice by leaving the country."
