    "chunk_text": "2,700 women-headed families in Mullaitivu\n\nMullaitivu District Secretary A. Umamaheswaran said, at a recent event organised by the Viluthu Foundation for Women to support women\u2019s livelihood and entrepreneurship, among the 47,000 families in Mullaitivu District, 2,700 families are entirely run by women, and more than 6,000 women are widows according to records.\n\nA participatory research on the definition of women heads of household conducted by Viluthu, the civil society organisation that supported in implementation of this livelihood effort found 11 main categories, and over 58 subcategories and more than 100 further sub divisions of women under the women heads of households banner- showing a lot more has to be done to understand their lived realities.\n\nA conservative estimate, without taking into consideration the actual definitions women have recommended suggests, there are at least 67,000 women-headed households across the Northern Province. They carry this responsibility in one of the poorest districts in the country, where household incomes sit well below the national average. The women and government social workers in the North and East estimate that if real inclusive definitions are used that there may be nearly 100,000 to 150,000 women heads of household in the North and East region alone. Mr. Umamaheswaran said how it is \u201cespecially the women\u2019s hard work that keeps families afloat. Primarily MSMEs in the district are run by women and it is their innovation and determination and effort that help their families, this community and this district.\u201d"
