    "chunk_size_bytes": 1796,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka clash headlines big sports day\n\nEngland will look to complete a 3-0 T20I series sweep when they face Sri Lanka in the third and final match at Old Trafford, Manchester, on September 19.\n\nHarry Brook\u2019s side have already secured an unassailable 2-0 lead after winning the second T20I by six wickets, leaving Sri Lanka with one final opportunity to finish the series with a victory.\n\nEngland head into the series finale in winning form, with Harry Brook leading their batting charts with 137 runs across the series. Liam Dawson has been their leading wicket-taker with five wickets.\n\nSri Lanka, meanwhile, will need a stronger all-round performance after struggling in the second encounter. Pathum Nissanka remains their leading run-scorer with 49 runs, while Wanindu Hasaranga has taken two wickets.\n\nBatting first in the second T20I, Sri Lanka managed 145 for nine in their 20 overs. Nissanka top-scored with 37, while Lahiru Udara contributed 21 off 20 balls.\n\nCharith Asalanka also made a start but failed to convert it into a substantial score. England\u2019s Liam Dawson claimed three wickets as Sri Lanka\u2019s lower order struggled to accelerate, leaving them with a below-par total.\n\nEngland\u2019s chase got off to a brisk start, with Jos Buttler scoring 30 off 16 balls and Aneurin Donald adding 21 from 13 deliveries.\n\nBrook chipped in with a quickfire 23 before Tom Banton took control of the chase, smashing an unbeaten 52 off just 24 balls.\n\nEngland reached the target in the 13th over, sealing a six-wicket victory and taking a 2-0 lead in the series.\n\nEngland: Harry Brook (c), Ben Duckett, James Coles, Will Jacks, Gus Atkinson, Liam Dawson, Jamie Overton, Tom Banton, Jos Buttler, Jordan Cox, Aneurin Donald, Jofra Archer, Sonny Baker, Saqib Mahmood, Josh Tongue, Adil Rashid."
  },
