    "chunk_size_bytes": 1274,
    "chunk_text": "The case was filed by the Police Financial Crimes Investigation Division and named several other accused. Basil\u2019s lawyers had previously informed court that he was overseas receiving medical treatment, while the court ordered that the arrest warrant be enforced after considering his repeated absence.\n\nAn Interpol Blue Notice is an international alert used by law enforcement to collect extra information about a person's identity, location, or activities in connection with a criminal investigation\n\nConversely, a Red Notice is sought for fugitives whose whereabouts remain entirely unknown. Sri Lanka's Interpol branch operates directly through the CID, which requests and processes these notices via the international INTERPOL Notices system.\n\n\u201cA Blue Notice has been issued for Basil Rajapaksa. When individuals are required for an investigation, we notify Interpol through a Blue Notice. If there is a known address showing he resides in a specific place, the Blue Notice conveys that he is required by the country,\u201d the minister said.\n\nThe Minister said the Government was taking the necessary legal and international steps to bring back individuals wanted in connection with criminal and bribery-related cases, regardless of their previous political positions."
