    "chunk_size_bytes": 2004,
    "chunk_text": "Ma Fiert\u00e9 partners Isle of Rataa  to introduce \u2018Duality\u2019\n\nLifestyle brand Ma Fiert\u00e9 has partnered with Isle of Rataa to present Duality, its latest collection of handcrafted leather and hand-painted artisanal teak pieces.\n\nThe collaboration marks a natural meeting of two design-led brands that share an appreciation for quality, individuality and the enduring value of craftsmanship.\n\nSince joining the Isle of Rataa portfolio in March, Ma Fiert\u00e9 has found a distinctive home for its work, with Duality now offering customers an opportunity to experience the collection within a carefully curated retail environment.\n\n\u201cMa Fiert\u00e9 has been a wonderful brand to work with at Isle of Rataa. Since joining us in March, the partnership has been effortless, with a shared appreciation for thoughtful design, quality and craftsmanship. Their new Duality collection is a beautiful expression of that,\u201d said Nilusha Shivaraj, Co-Founder, Isle of Rataa.\n\n\u201cThe interplay of hand painted teak and leather creates pieces that are both distinctive and beautifully considered, with a quiet sophistication that makes them easy to live with. We\u2019re delighted to have Duality in store and to give our customers the opportunity to experience the collection for themselves,\u201d she added.\n\nAt the heart of Duality is an exploration of the relationship between utility and artistry. The collection brings together hand-painted teak creations alongside everyday luxury pieces including work-ready laptop sleeves, structured laptop bags and refined leather wallets.\n\n\u201cWith Duality, we set out to honor the gap between the everyday essentials we rely on and the statement art pieces that elevate special moments. By pairing hand painted artisanal teak designs alongside everyday luxury items like work-ready laptop sleeves, structured laptop bags, and sleek leather wallets, this collection ensures you never have to choose between utility and craftsmanship,\u201d said SafraAnver, Marketing Director at Ma Fiert\u00e9."
