    "md5": "2f014076a0720ccb033d13c064bf96e2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1999,
    "chunk_text": "DFCC Aloka inspires future leaders\n\nDFCC Bank, through its women-focused banking proposition DFCC Aloka, supported Avenza, an exclusive professional educational summit designed to inspire the students awaiting state university admission and help them prepare for the next stage of their academic and professional journeys.\n\nThe summit, organised by renowned ICT educator Bhanuka Ekanayake, brought together 350 students for a programme focused on learning, personal development, leadership, innovation and opportunity.\n\nDFCC Aloka\u2019s participation added a professional and leadership perspective to the forum, encouraging the students to think beyond the academic achievement and prepare for the wider demands of the future workplace.\n\nDFCC Bank Vice President and Pinnacle and Aloka Proposition Head Shera Hassen was invited as a distinguished guest speaker at the summit. In her session, she shared practical insights on leadership, embracing opportunity, continuous learning and building the confidence needed to navigate academic and career transitions.\n\nThe engagement reflects DFCC Bank\u2019s broader focus on supporting growth-oriented communities by contributing to knowledge-sharing platforms that benefit future generations.\n\nAt a time when young people are entering higher education and preparing for careers in a rapidly changing economy, exposure to industry perspectives can help them make more informed choices and develop a stronger sense of direction.\n\nHassen said, \u201cStudents awaiting university admission are at an important point in their lives. The choices they make, the habits they build and the opportunities they choose to pursue can shape the way they contribute to society and the economy in the years ahead. Platforms such as Avenza give young people the space to think boldly, learn from different perspectives and prepare themselves with confidence. Through DFCC Aloka, we are pleased to support initiatives that encourage leadership, ambition and lifelong learning.\u201d"
  },
