    "chunk_size_bytes": 2004,
    "chunk_text": "Beverlee Holdings redefines property development in Thalahena\n\nBeverlee Holdings (Pvt.) Ltd is redefining property development in Thalahena through its multi-unit residential project, highlighting the company\u2019s growing contribution to Sri Lanka\u2019s property development and construction sector.\n\nThe project reflects Beverlee Holdings\u2019 end-to-end design-and-build service, bringing land assessment, architectural design, structural engineering, interior design, project coordination and final handover under one roof.\n\nFor the customers, this means a more convenient process with fewer parties to coordinate and clearer accountability from start to finish, showcasing the company\u2019s signature \u2018design-and-build\u2019 approach. Beverlee Holdings has completed over 70 such projects across Sri Lanka.\n\nOperating continuously for close to two decades, Beverlee Holdings has developed expertise across residential developments, commercial spaces, retrofits and hospitality-focused projects. Its Thalahena initiative reflects the company\u2019s broader approach to adding value with carefully finished living environments.\n\n\u201cClients want a smoother way to manage property development without having to coordinate several separate contractors. Our model brings the key stages together, from design and engineering to construction and finishing, so the process is clearer and more convenient. The same approach guides our boutique villa projects along the Hiriketiya-Dickwella coastal belt, where we are combining modern luxury with Sri Lanka\u2019s tropical setting,\u201d said Beverlee Holdings Managing Director Bemal Gamage.\n\nThe company\u2019s services include sustainable design and build, property development, architectural design, interior design, refurbishment and real estate investment. The integrated model gives their clients a single point of responsibility throughout the development process. Beverlee Holdings continues to focus on craftsmanship, practical pricing and disciplined project management."
