    "chunk_size_bytes": 660,
    "chunk_text": "In February this year, there was another controversy as the Bangladeshi Cricket Board (BCB)\u00a0 requested their T20 World Cup Tournament games scheduled to be played in India be shifted to Sri Lanka\u00a0 citing security concerns due to growing tensions between the countries.\n\nICC rejected the request. After being given a final deadline to play in India, the BCB refused to travel, and\u00a0 ICC\u00a0 replaced Bangladesh with Scotland.\u00a0 Bangladesh felt poorly treated.\n\nBut then again these \u2018outdated\u2019 rules and traditions were made at a time when cricket was played for the joy of\u00a0 the game. Today cricket has become a well-paid job and is played as an occupation."
