    "md5": "a99625620302f0c80189dc04f99b7047",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 831,
    "chunk_text": "Rainfall expected to increase in southwestern areas\n\nColombo, Sep.19 (Daily Mirror) - Rainfall in the southwestern parts of the country is expected to increase over the next few days from today (19), the Meteorology Department said.\n\nShowers are expected at times in the Western, Sabaragamuwa and North-Western provinces, as well as in the Galle, Matara, Kandy and Nuwara Eliya districts.\n\nThe Department said some areas in Sabaragamuwa Province and the Kandy and Nuwara Eliya districts could receive moderate to heavy rainfall exceeding 50 mm.\n\nShowers or thundershowers are also likely in parts of Uva Province and the Mullaitivu, Batticaloa and Ampara districts after 2 p.m.\n\nThe public has been advised to take necessary precautions to minimise risks from temporary strong winds and lightning that may accompany thundershowers."
