    "chunk_id": "2026-09-19-dailymirrorlk-4c64f6ac-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "77722ea90f298c46e7d90d017edfce4e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1612,
    "chunk_text": "Trump announces \u2018permanent\u2019 US security control over Greenland\n\nWASHINGTON -\u00a0 US President Donald Trump has announced that the United States has reached an agreement with Denmark and Greenland that he says gives Washington permanent control over security and other needs in Greenland.\n\nTrump made the announcement in a post on his official X account, saying the agreement would give the US the \u201ccomplete ability\u201d to take necessary measures to secure and defend Greenland and the United States.\n\n> \u201cThe United States of America has entered into an Agreement with The Kingdom of Denmark, and Greenland, that gives the United States permanent control over security, and all other needs, in Greenland, completely addressing ALL of our many U.S. concerns,\u201d Trump said.\n\nHe said there would be \u201cNO COST\u201d to the United States under the agreement and claimed that no US adversary would be able to establish a base, maintain a military presence or make sensitive investments in Greenland without Washington\u2019s written approval.\n\nTrump also said the US would immediately begin developing a larger military presence at suitable locations in Greenland.\n\nDescribing the arrangement as an \u201cInfinite Life\u201d Agreement, Trump said it would have no end and called the development \u201chistoric\u201d and \u201cspecial.\u201d\n\nHe said the US would work with the people of Greenland on the development and construction of the military presence.\n\nThe announcement comes amid longstanding US interest in Greenland\u2019s strategic importance in the Arctic and Trump\u2019s previous calls for greater US control over the territory."
  },
