    "chunk_text": "Aircraft tracking website Flightradar24 said on Saturday that Riyadh\u2019s airport was facing major problems. It placed the airport at its highest disruption level, 5.0, which the site describes as long delays and several flights being cancelled. The disruption wasn\u2019t limited to Riyadh itself flights to and from Dubai and Sharjah were also hit as a knock-on result of the issues at King Khalid International Airport.\n\nAl-Malki said the Houthis also tried to target the cities of Baish, Taif, Farasan and Yanbu, but that these attempts were stopped by air defence systems. He said the coalition holds the right to respond in line with international humanitarian law to deter further attacks.\n\nSaudi Arabia and the Houthi movement in Yemen have been on opposing sides of Yemen\u2019s long-running conflict for years, with the Saudi-led coalition backing Yemen\u2019s internationally recognised government. Riyadh had issued an overnight air raid alert for the second time this weekend, the first such alert since fighting in Yemen intensified this month.\n\nThe coalition has repeatedly said Houthi attacks are aimed at civilian areas rather than military targets, a claim the group denies. Saturday\u2019s missile and drone activity, and the disruption it caused at Riyadh\u2019s airport, is the latest flashpoint in that ongoing standoff."
