    "chunk_size_bytes": 766,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lankan model wins third place at Top Model of Universe\n\nColombo, Sep. 20 (Daily Mirror) - Sri Lankan model Savinda Tennakoon, who represented the country at the \u201cTop Model of Universe - 2026\u201d competition in Turkey, returned to Sri Lanka after securing third place and winning the Best National Costume award.\n\nThe competition was held in Istanbul from September 14 to 18, with models from 33 countries participating.\n\nTennakoon arrived at the Bandaranaike International Airport in Katunayake at around 5.10 a.m. today (20), aboard Turkish Airlines flight TK-730.\n\nHis parents and the National Director of the competition, Mayura Perera, were present at the airport to welcome him.\n\nTennakoon is currently studying Computer Science at a university in England."
