    "md5": "5aa5f738c33b9309bc00b78d51d81120",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1583,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka seeks stronger China-South Asia Ocean cooperation\n\nColombo, Sep. 20 (Daily Mirror) - Sri Lanka is fully prepared to further strengthen long-term, practical cooperation with China and South Asian nations across key sectors, including marine science, fisheries, aquaculture, the blue economy, technology, investments, and human resource development, Minister of Fisheries, Aquatic, and Ocean Resources Ramalingam Chandrasekar announced.\n\nDelivering the keynote address at the opening of the \"China\u2013South Asian Countries Marine Cooperation Forum\" held on September 17 and 18 in the Qingdao West Coast New Area, the Minister emphasized Sri Lanka\u2019s commitment to sustainable ocean governance. Minister Chandrasekar attended the event during a three-day official visit to China following a formal invitation from Zexun Wei, Director General of the First Institute of Oceanography under China's Ministry of Natural Resources.\n\nThe high-level forum brought together over 100 government officials, experts, and academics from China, Sri Lanka, Bangladesh, the Maldives, and Pakistan. Key discussions centered on climate change, marine environmental protection, ocean disaster monitoring, early warning systems, disaster risk reduction, and capacity building. The Sri Lankan delegation accompanying the Minister included Ministry Secretary Dr. B.K. Kolitha Kamal Jinadasa, National Aquatic Resources Research and Development Agency (NARA) Chairman Dr. Sanath Hettiarachchi, NARA Director General Dr. K.H.M.L. Amaralal, and Senior Oceanography Researcher Dr. W.N.C. Priyadarshani."
  },
