    "language": "en",
    "md5": "c4e8f0d6d5ea7711fb52f60301ec9a02",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1751,
    "chunk_text": "DMASL to host Digital Summit Asia/Sri Lanka next month\n\nFrom left: Vice Presidents of the Digital Marketing Association of Sri Lanka and the Co-Chairs of Digital Summit Asia 2026 Shalendra Mendis and Gayathri Seneviratne (individual cards), Chairman, Sri Lanka Convention Bureau and Sri Lanka Institute of Tourism and Hotel Management Dheera Hettiarachchi, Chairman, Sri Lanka Tourism Promotion Bureau Buddhika Hewawasam, President - Digital Marketing Association of Sri Lanka Arjun Jeger, Nirojan Yogeswaran - Marketing Manager - The Lotus Tower Colombo, Treasurer - Digital Marketing Association of Sri Lanka Muhammed Gazzaly\n\nDigital Marketers Association of Sri Lanka (DMASL) is set to host Digital Summit Asia/Sri Lanka 2026, on 1st and 2nd October at Water\u2019s Edge, Colombo.\n\nPowered by Visa, the Summit will bring together leading voices from across Asia\u2019s digital, marketing, creative, technology and business communities.\n\nMarking a new chapter for the Summit, this year\u2019s event expands its focus beyond Sri Lanka to create a regional platform for ideas, collaboration and exchange, connecting local professionals with creators, innovators, entrepreneurs and industry leaders from across Asia.\n\nUnder the theme \u201cThe Epicentre\u201d, the 2026 Summit explores how new ideas, perspective sand possibilities emerge when different minds and disciplines come together.\n\nThe Summit\u2019s central idea is built around a new epicentre of creativity, technology and intelligence, bringing together the people and communities shaping what comes next.\n\nFrom creators and entrepreneurs to marketers, technology leaders and business professionals, Digital Summit Asia aims to create new conversations and connections that extend beyond the two-day event."
  },
