    "chunk_size_bytes": 1524,
    "chunk_text": "Hutch secures back-to-back Gold\n\nHutch has secured a Gold award, a Black Dragon and a Silver award at Dragons of Sri Lanka 2026, a prestigious marketing communications and advertising awards ceremony recognising regional creative excellence, strategic campaigns and brand achievements.\n\nHutch stood out as the only telecommunications brand honoured at this year\u2019s ceremony, with all three accolades developed in partnership with TBWA\\Sri Lanka.\n\nThe key highlight is the Gold award for Best Use of Artificial Intelligence (AI), awarded for \u2018The Roaming Hack\u2019, a campaign for Hutch\u2019s industry-leading roaming proposition that used AI to rethink how the customers experience roaming. The same campaign also earned a Black Dragon under a further award category.\n\nHutch also earned a Silver award for Best Product Launch, awarded for \u2018Hutch Pissuwak Ma Thamai\u2019, the campaign behind the Hutch 15 Apps product. The recognition reflects the campaign\u2019s ability to combine sharp creative storytelling with a distinctive product proposition to capture customer attention.\n\nHutch\u2019s triple win at Dragons of Sri Lanka reflects the brand\u2019s growing strength in combining technology, creative excellence and customer insight to create campaigns that deliver meaningful impact and resonance amongst diverse audiences.\n\nThe recognition reinforces Hutch as a brand that pairs innovation with creativity, at a time when the company continues to extract value from AI and data-driven decisioning across its business functions."
