    "chunk_text": "DFCC Bank-SLBFE help migrant workers turn overseas earnings into homes\n\n\u2018Ethera Diriya\u2019 housing loan scheme offers eligible migrant workers up to Rs.10mn, with an interest reimbursement facility\n\nDFCC Bank has partnered with the Sri Lanka Bureau of Foreign Employment (SLBFE) to introduce the \u2018Ethera Diriya\u2019 housing loan scheme, helping the Sri Lankan migrant workers invest their overseas earnings in a home and greater long-term security for their families.\n\nThe memorandum of understanding was signed by DFCC Bank Vice President and Head of Products and Propositions, Retail and Business Banking Asitha Pinnaduwa and SLBFE Chairman Koshala Wickramasinghe.\n\nUnder the scheme, the eligible Sri Lankan migrant workers can obtain housing loans of up to Rs.10 million, with the repayment periods of up to 10 years. The financing can be used to construct, purchase, renovate or improve a residential property.\n\nThe scheme also includes an interest reimbursement mechanism facilitated by the SLBFE. The eligible borrowers will receive financial relief through the applicable interest subsidy, helping make the cost of homeownership more manageable.\n\nFor Sri Lankans working overseas, owning a home represents more than acquiring property. It is an opportunity to turn years of work away from home into something lasting for the families waiting for them.\n\n\u201cHundreds of thousands of Sri Lankans work overseas to create a better future for their families. Their earnings support their loved ones and make an important contribution to the national economy. Through Ethera Diriya, we want to help them convert that effort into a secure home and an asset that will serve their families for years,\u201d said Pinnaduwa."
