    "md5": "cd4ff70387e281e310dc6cbaab0a7683",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 872,
    "chunk_text": "In other words, I claim that the consequences of another bond market crash or the AI bubble bursting will be far worse than the previous financial crises. The confluence of crisis tendencies may create a downward cycle of unravelling that even the Central Banks and Finance Ministries of the most powerful countries will be unable to address; all the more so, as these states are at loggerheads with each other. This global political situation is more akin to the situation in the 1930s, when the resolution to the crisis came only after a prolonged depression, the rise of fascism and a devastating world war.\n\nMost of all, we need to shore up our resources and secure the essential needs for our people starting with food security. In a dangerously shifting world, when amnesia of past crises is the norm, are we ready to change our thinking and the economic trajectory?"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
