    "md5": "92cce0cd3c2a727afee77394adf35dc3",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1621,
    "chunk_text": "Sivarasa Anojan:  Sri Lanka must not lose another citizen\n\nA reported death sentence in Saudi Arabia, unanswered questions surrounding an appeal, and the memory of Rizana Nafeek demand urgent action \u2014 and careful diplomacy\n\nWhen a human life may be at stake, there is simply no room for delay; clemency must accompany, rather than substitute for, the strongest legal defence\n\nNever again should one of our citizens reach the final stages of a capital case overseas without competent legal representation, proper interpretation, and full state engagement\n\nThe reported death sentence imposed on Sri Lankan migrant worker Sivarasa Anojan in Saudi Arabia over a social media comment demands immediate legal action and high-level diplomatic intervention. Drawing painful parallels to the tragic execution of Rizana Nafeek, Sri Lanka cannot afford bureaucratic delays, procedural lapses, or uncoordinated legal defense. The government must act with absolute urgency\u2014ensuring competent counsel, competent translation, and strategic appeals for clemency\u2014to respect Saudi sovereignty while utilizing every possible avenue to bring another vulnerable Sri Lankan citizen home alive.\n\nA mother in Narpittimunai is waiting for news that she prays will never come. Her son, Sivarasa Anojan, a Sri Lankan migrant worker in Saudi Arabia, was sentenced by a Saudi court on 15 July to five years\u2019 imprisonment and a fine of SAR 3 million over a social media comment reportedly deemed insulting to Islam and the Prophet Muhammad. His family has subsequently been told that the punishment was increased to death following an appeal."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
