    "time_ut": 1789944144.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-09-21-dailymirrorlk-487e9f89-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "050561c8bccd7eaf3e6b4017ac25f923",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1870,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka navigates path to implement  out-of-country voting\n\nEven though OCV was discussed during the 2024 Presidential Election, Sri Lanka is still in its preliminary stages\n\nTwo-day regional conference held in Colombo to discuss persisting challenges regarding voting rights for overseas Sri Lankans\n\nInstrument that addresses political participation of immigrants is the Intl. Convention for the Rights of Migrant Workers\n\nDespite having over 1.5 million citizens working overseas, Sri Lanka is one among many South Asian countries that is yet to implement Out-of-Country Voting (OCV). Studies indicate that in South Asia, millions of people relocate annually due to factors driven by employment, education, family circumstances, safety concerns or environmental pressures. But, apart from a few exceptions, electoral frameworks across the region require people to be physically present at the polling station on the day of the election. Even though OCV was discussed during the 2024 Presidential Election, Sri Lanka is still in its preliminary stages. In this backdrop, a two-day regional conference was recently held in Colombo to discuss international best practices and persisting challenges regarding voting rights for overseas Sri Lankans.\n\nAt this conference, jointly organised by the Elections Commission of Sri Lanka and the International Foundation for Electoral Systems (IFES), representatives from Australia, Bangladesh, Maldives, Nepal and the Philippines shared their practical experiences and successful mechanisms for securing voting rights for citizens living abroad.\n\nModern democracies are evolving and human mobility is reshaping societies, economies and political systems across the globe. There was a time when elections were conducted within the boundaries of countries. People\u2019s democratic rights too were exercised within these boundaries."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-09-21-dailymirrorlk-487e9f89",
    "num": "dailymirrorlk-487e9f89",
    "date_str": "2026-09-21",
    "description": "Sri Lanka navigates path to implement  out-of-country voting",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/news-features/Sri-Lanka-navigates-path-to-implement-out-of-country-voting/131-350764",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
