    "md5": "09be2aa92c5de404abac103b26ca3569",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1913,
    "chunk_text": "Sister of Pakistan\u2019s ex-PM Imran Khan arrested\n\nBBC - The sister of Pakistan's imprisoned former prime minister, Imran Khan, has been arrested ahead of next week's protests held in his support, his Pakistan Tehreek-e-Insaf (PTI) party has said.\n\nAleema Khanum was detained in the eastern city of Lahore on Sunday afternoon, PTI officials said, calling it an \"illegal detention\". Her son is demanding her return.\n\nThe order for Khanum's arrest, which came from Lahore's deputy commissioner, alleged that she was mobilising Imran Khan's supporters \"through social media and public meetings\". It added that she will be detained for 30 days.\n\nKhanum is a vocal critic of her brother's detention, regularly speaking to his supporters and the media.\n\nA police official confirmed Khanum's arrest to the BBC. According to the order, she will be taken to Kot Lakhpat jail in Lahore.\n\nEarlier in the day, her family said they had had \"no contact or news of her whereabouts\".\n\n\"We demand the government immediately disclose her whereabouts and ensure her safe return,\" Khanum's son Shahrez Khan wrote on X.\n\nMany have linked her arrest to the protests that have been organised across the country on 27 September, when demonstrators plan to march to the Pakistani capital, Islamabad.\n\nThe arrest order said Khanum had been mobilising people to \"create law and order situations\" and \"raising/chanting objectionable slogans amongst the general public against the Government.\"\n\nStreets in Islamabad are already lined with shipping containers, ready to safeguard the city's government buildings.\n\nLocal media has reported Pakistan's interior minister as saying that the protests harm the country and that the government will do everything they can to stop them.\n\nKhan has been detained since 2023, when he was sentenced to three years in prison for not declaring money earned from selling gifts he had received while in office."
  },
