    "chunk_text": "The gap suggests that digital access is increasingly taking place through mobile devices rather than traditional personal computers. Smartphones accounted for 80.6% of device usage recorded in the survey, while desktop and laptop computers accounted for 17.4%.\n\nAt provincial level, Western Province recorded the highest computer literacy rate at 50.2%, while North Central Province recorded the lowest at 24.3%.\n\nThe overall computer literacy rate of 39.2% represented a 3.3 percentage-point increase from 2024.\n\nThe survey defines a computer-literate person as someone aged 5\u201369 who is able to use a computer on their own.\n\nThe DCS has conducted computer literacy surveys periodically since 2004, with a survey module attached to the Sri Lanka Labour Force Survey from 2014 onwards."
