    "chunk_size_bytes": 1171,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cWe allocated Rs. 600 billion to provide fuel concessions in April, May, June and July. The Government must give a concession if fuel prices are increased unbearably,\u201d he said.\n\nThe President said the Government was also giving priority to the development of education, health and transport.\n\nHe added that the Government was placing particular emphasis on digitalization, with plans to construct 1,000 communication towers within three years. Funds would be allocated for 750 towers next year, he said.\n\nPresident Dissanayake also highlighted the Government's islandwide public rallies and consultations covering various sectors, including women and youth, saying they were intended to strengthen engagement between the Government and the people.\n\n\u201cThe rulers must be responsible for the people. If the rulers are not directed on the correct path, people have a right to protest. We need to ensure full democracy. We cannot move forward by suppressing the media or contracting democracy,\u201d he said.\n\nThe President further claimed that public approval of the Government had increased compared with the level of support it had received when it first assumed office."
