    "chunk_text": "Dr. Sanjeewa said the NMRA and the State Pharmaceuticals Corporation (SPC), which imported the medicines, should explain how the consignment was brought into the country and subsequently released from Customs. He also accused responsible officials of withholding information while cancer patients and doctors faced difficulties over the availability and administration of medicines.\n\nAccording to him, doctors at several hospitals have raised concerns on social media over problems associated with the continued administration of certain medicines to cancer patients.\n\nHe also raised concerns over shortages of doctors and specialists in the public health system, claiming that delays in approving the required cadre positions and salary and tax-related issues were discouraging doctors from joining the public service.\n\nHe said the continued migration of young doctors overseas was also affecting the health sector.\n\nDr. Sanjeewa claimed that the health service should have at least around 5,000 specialists and 30,000 medical officers, but that delays in Treasury approval of the required cadre had created further difficulties.\n\nThe allegations could not be independently verified, and the NMRA and SPC have not been given as having responded to the claims.\n\nCancer patients pushed towards costly private treatment amid treatment delays"
