    "chunk_size_bytes": 990,
    "chunk_text": "China\u2019s Xi to visit the US from September 23-25\n\nReuters - Chinese President Xi Jinping \u200bwill pay a state visit \u200cto the US from September 23 to 25 at the invitation of President Donald Trump, \u200bChina's Foreign Ministry said \u200bin a statement on Monday.\n\nDuring the \u2060visit, Xi \"will hold in-depth exchanges \u200bof views with President Trump on \u200bmajor issues concerning China-US relations, as well as world peace and development,\" a Chinese \u200bforeign ministry spokesperson said during \u200ba regular press conference shortly after the \u200cannouncement.\n\nThe \u2060reciprocal visits by the two heads of state within a six-month period are \"of historic, milestone significance,\" ministry \u200bspokesperson Guo \u200bJiakun \u2060said.\n\n\"China is willing to work with the US to ... strengthen dialogue and \u200bcooperation, properly manage differences, \u200bcontinuously \u2060enhance the well-being of the peoples of both countries, and promote world \u2060peace, \u200bstability and prosperity,\" \u200bGuo added."
