    "md5": "606a489057978a9e717b4ebc00a6f9b3",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 853,
    "chunk_text": "Vijitha Herath to make special statement in Parliament on Sivarasa Anojan\n\nColombo, Sep. 21 (Daily Mirror) - Foreign Minister Vijitha Herath is scheduled to make a special statement in Parliament tomorrow regarding the case of Sri Lankan national Sivarasa Anojan, who has been sentenced to death in Saudi Arabia.\n\nMinister Herath confirmed to the Daily Mirror that he would address Parliament on the matter tomorrow.\n\nThe Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism earlier said it was closely monitoring Anojan\u2019s case, which is currently undergoing judicial proceedings in Saudi Arabia.\n\nPresident Anura Kumara Dissanayake and Minister Herath met the parents of Sivarasa Anojan this morning and assured them that the Government was making every possible effort to secure a pardon for Anojan through both legal and diplomatic channels."
