    "md5": "eddc51a763cad33e1ac531be9688bbb9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 648,
    "chunk_text": "Resus Energy commissions 2 MW Ampara solar plant\n\nResus Energy PLC kicked off the commercial operations at a new two megawatt (MW) solar power plant in Ampara, expanding the renewable energy producer\u2019s generation portfolio.\n\nThe facility, located in Damana, was commissioned on September 18 and is expected to generate about 3.5 gigawatt-hours of electricity annually for supply to the national grid, the company said in a filing to the Colombo Stock Exchange.\n\nThe projected output implies an average capacity factor of about 20 percent.\n\nThe plant was developed through Resus Eastern Solar (Pvt.) Ltd, a wholly-owned subsidiary of Resus Energy."
