    "md5": "a26353b6a5ece2ea7635b9c69efee351",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1083,
    "chunk_text": "Inflation more than triples in 7 months\n\nLatest increase puts inflation at its highest level so far in 2026 and signals a marked reversal from subdued price environment at beginning of year\n\nNon-food inflation, which has been running considerably higher, edged up further to 9.3%, from 9.2% in July\n\nInflation has more than tripled in just seven months, climbing to 8.1 percent in August, as a sharp resurgence in food prices added to the already elevated household costs, the official data showed.\n\nThe National Consumer Price Index (NCPI) inflation accelerated from 7.2 percent in July and 2.4 percent in January, extending an almost uninterrupted rise in the headline rate this year.\n\nThis latest increase puts inflation at its highest level so far in 2026 and signals a marked reversal from the subdued price environment at the beginning of the year.\n\nThe NCPI inflation trajectory has risen from 2.4 percent in January to 1.6 percent in February, 2.4 percent in March, 4.7 percent in April, 5.4 percent in May, 6.5 percent in June, 7.2 percent in July and 8.1 percent in August."
  },
