    "md5": "da47f6adc09f3ac9eb0e8f083edc3507",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 898,
    "chunk_text": "133 construction workers to leave for Israel tomorrow\n\nColombo, Sep. 22 (Daily Mirror) - A total of 133 Sri Lankan construction job seekers are scheduled to leave for Israel tomorrow (23) for employment in the country\u2019s construction sector, the Sri Lanka Bureau of Foreign Employment (SLBFE) said.\n\nAn awareness programme for job seekers selected for employment in the Israeli construction and infrastructure sectors, along with the distribution of air tickets, was held at the SLBFE auditorium on September 14 under the patronage of SLBFE Chairman Kosala Wickramasinghe.\n\nAir tickets were distributed to 133 job seekers bound for employment in the construction sector and 17 job seekers selected for jobs in the infrastructure sector.\n\nThe programme was aimed at providing the prospective migrant workers with necessary information and guidance ahead of their departure for employment in Israel."
