    "description": "FiNAC HR Optimizer more relevant today: Datamation Chief",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/business-news/FiNAC-HR-Optimizer-more-relevant-today-Datamation-Chief/273-350924",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1790123566.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-09-23-dailymirrorlk-293736b5-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "8e91963478a0ba8dc429459313be3b9a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1909,
    "chunk_text": "FiNAC HR Optimizer more relevant today: Datamation Chief\n\nWith work models of both private companies and government institutions shifting dramatically toward flexible, tech-driven and human-centred forms, \u2018governance\u2019 has become a key requirement for business success.\n\nAccording to a prominent Sri Lankan software development company, workforce management software (WFM) has emerged as an indispensable tool for streamlining processes and improving productivity and by deploying the right WFM software containing strong controls, organisations can reduce operational costs, boost employee engagement and position themselves for long-term success in a competitive market. \u201cMost banks and large businesses today run hybrid or remote teams; that\u2019s not a passing phase; it\u2019s simply how work happens now. The problem is the way most companies price work, staff projects and prove compliance was built for a world where everyone sat in one building. Nobody notices the gap until a project quietly slips or a regulator asks for evidence that doesn\u2019t exist,\u201d said Datamation Systems (Pvt.) Ltd Chairman and Managing Director Fazal Issadeen.\n\n\u2018FiNAC HR Optimizer\u2019, the workforce management software developed by Datamation, is more relevant today, because the working model has changed globally and most companies\u2019 governance model hasn\u2019t caught up or adapted to that change.\n\n\u201cThat\u2019s exactly why it should be seen as an investment, not a cost. The real cost is the one you can\u2019t see right now: idle time, a project quietly running over budget, an office bigger than the business actually needs. HR Optimizer doesn\u2019t add that cost; it makes it visible, so leadership can act on it,\u201d added Issadeen, the Chief Architect of HR Optimizer.\n\nHe further said that there\u2019s a second kind of cost hiding in the same blind spot: a fraud case or a data leak with no evidence trail to answer it."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-09-23-dailymirrorlk-293736b5",
    "num": "dailymirrorlk-293736b5",
    "date_str": "2026-09-23",
    "description": "FiNAC HR Optimizer more relevant today: Datamation Chief",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/business-news/FiNAC-HR-Optimizer-more-relevant-today-Datamation-Chief/273-350924",
