    "chunk_text": "Delivering the keynote address on \u201cThe Role of CEOs in Leading Institutional Transformation,\u201d Dr. Kishu Gomes called on industry leaders to approach the coming regulatory transition as an opportunity to strengthen governance and rebuild public trust in the sector, rather than treating it as a constraint on growth.\n\nIn recognition of his long-standing service to the country\u2019s microfinance movement, the forum conferred Honorary Membership of LMFN upon G. Victor Rathnayake.\n\nThe event was supported by LCB Finance PLC as Finance Partner, represented by its Chief Executive Officer Leelananda, and M-CRIL Limited as LMFN\u2019s International Knowledge Partner, represented by Chief Executive Officer Sudhir Narayan and AVP \u2013 Inclusive Finance Abhinav Ashesh. Evoke Labs served as IT Partner, while Liyasi TV was the Television Partner.\n\nFormal proceedings were followed by a networking dinner, which offered participants an informal setting to continue discussions on collaboration and the sector\u2019s direction.\n\nLMFN is the largest and most inclusive microfinance network in Sri Lanka, works to strengthen the sector through advocacy, capacity building and engagement with policymakers and regulators."
