    "language": "en",
    "md5": "8b9b0b2c1cc7d030e0d9efc3cd4b4ed3",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1860,
    "chunk_text": "AKD\u2019s two years and beyond\n\nPresident Anura Kumara Dissanayake completes two years in office today, seemingly with satisfaction of his thus far performance and perhaps with uncertainty over the future.\n\nAlthough former Presidents Ranasinghe Premadasa and Maithripala Sirisena also hailed from ordinary backgrounds, they had been elevated to the elite class when they assumed power. However, it was Dissanayake who will go down in history as the first leader to come from both a working-class family and a remarkably humble background even when assuming power.\n\nIn fact, the rise of the National People\u2019s Power (NPP), Dissanayake\u2019s party,\u00a0 is in a way accidental and it was former President Gotabaya Rajapaksa and his political clan that created a conducive environment for it.\n\nMarxism, Dissanayake\u2019s original political doctrine,\u00a0 observes that revolutions cannot be won without a revolutionary environment being created by the history. Gotabaya created it, while his brother Mahinda Rajapaksa \u2014 who boasted about his experience in governance \u2014 praised it during an interview with the Daily Mirror, calling it a fantastic job.\n\nPressured by the miles-long and weeks-long queues for fuel and cooking gas and a thirteen-hour power cut as a result of\u00a0 mismanagement by the Gotabaya Rajapaksa government, millions of people marched to the capital on April, 2022 and camped in front of President\u2019s office, ultimately forcing him to flee\u00a0 the country.\n\nAlthough International Monetary Fund (IMF) guided the country towards a relative recovery during the Ranil Wickremesinghe administration, people\u2019s anger towards the highly corrupt Rajapaksa regime, and later towards Wickremesinghe for collaborating with the Rajapaksas,\u00a0 created the \u201crevolutionary environment\u201d favourabe to the NPP, at the next Presidential and general elections in 2024."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-09-23-dailymirrorlk-31f6cf74",
    "num": "dailymirrorlk-31f6cf74",
    "date_str": "2026-09-23",
    "description": "AKD\u2019s two years and beyond",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/opinion/AKDs-two-years-and-beyond/172-350940",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
