    "md5": "dd46255369d2f5544afbc14c64eaeba3",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1859,
    "chunk_text": "Easter Sunday Attack Verdict:  More a moment of reckoning than a closure\n\nIn the end,\u00a0 suicide bombers struck after\u00a0 local authorities disregarded multiple intelligence warnings by the Indian intelligence agencies\n\nThe judgement should provide closure to the survivors, the family members and the nation at large\n\nOn April 21, 2019, nine suicide bombers belonging to a home-grown Islamist extremist group, Jamathei Millathu Ibraheem (JMI), struck multiple churches and upscale hotels, killing 270 worshippers and tourists, and wounding five hundred people\n\nAt the time of this writing on Tuesday, a Trial-at-Bar of the Colombo High Court was expected to deliver the verdict on the landmark trial on the Easter Sunday terrorist attacks in 2019.\n\nIn one of the most exhaustive court cases,\u00a0 the trial had 2,309 witnesses testify on behalf of the prosecution and a total of 23,270 charges filed against the 24 accused. One accused died in prison.\n\nAmong the accused were Mohammed Naufar alias Naufar Mavilavi, whom the FBI identified as the second emir of an Islamist cell, that pledged allegiance to the Islamic State, Mohamed Anwar Mohamed Riksan and Ahmed Milan Hayathu Mohamed. All three suspects were earlier indicted by the FBI for conspiring to provide material support to a designated foreign terrorist organisation.\n\nThe judgement should provide closure to the survivors, the family members and the nation at large. It should also be a moment of reckoning and retrospection, even more so now given that the tragedy had now been politicised to the extent that it threatens to blind the nation of repetition.\n\nOn April 21, 2019, nine suicide bombers belonging to a home-grown Islamist extremist group, Jamathei Millathu Ibraheem (JMI), struck multiple churches and upscale hotels, killing 270 worshippers and tourists, and wounding five hundred people."
