    "md5": "f9755343ba61515a67d58732c577e167",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 947,
    "chunk_text": "Counsel submitted that the accused had children who were affected by their incarceration. The first accused had two sons from a previous marriage, while a seven-year-old daughter from her present marriage had also been placed in a child care home. The second accused, a three-wheeler driver, was described as the sole breadwinner of the family and had responsibility for his mother and university-going sister.\n\nThe Court observed that sentencing involves consideration of several factors, including the circumstances in which an offence was committed. It referred to previous judicial decisions emphasising the seriousness of an offence, deterrence, protection of the community and rehabilitation among the considerations relevant to sentencing.\n\nAccordingly, the Court reduced the sentence on each count to four years\u2019 rigorous imprisonment, to run concurrently. The fines and compensation orders imposed by the High Court were left unchanged."
