    "md5": "0e8cafdc0f2c943d3993691a5d4af358",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1969,
    "chunk_text": "He said various ideas and perceptions had developed in Sri Lankan society regarding foreign employment, while Israel had currently become a highly sought-after destination among Sri Lankan workers due to the demand in the Israeli labour market and comparatively high salaries.\n\nHe also rejected the claim that the number of employment opportunities received from the Israeli Government had decreased because such jobs were being channelled through private employment agencies.\n\nAccording to Wickramasinghe, around 300,000 Sri Lankans leave the country annually for foreign employment through legal channels.\n\nWith Government intervention, around 5,000 Sri Lankans leave for employment in Israel, another 5,000 for South Korea and around 1,000 for Japan annually.\n\nHe said the total number of Sri Lankans who had gone abroad for employment was around 125,000, of whom only about 11,000 had been sent through Government intervention, while the remaining 114,000 had secured employment through registered employment agencies and self-directed arrangements.\n\nWickramasinghe said legally sent remittances from migrant workers were a major factor in strengthening the country's economy and that the Government would make every effort to develop Sri Lanka's foreign labour force for the country's future.\n\nHe said the public should clearly understand that the main responsibility of the SLBFE was to regulate the process of overseas employment and ensure the welfare of migrant workers rather than simply sending people abroad.\n\nThe Chairman also said the Bureau had introduced several new welfare measures for migrant workers.\n\nHe said housing loans ranging from Rs.500,000 to Rs.1 million had recently been made available to migrant workers registered with the Bureau who had returned to Sri Lanka after working overseas.\n\nHe added that steps were being taken to introduce a concessionary programme through the relevant fund to assist with payment of interest on such loans."
