    "chunk_text": "Ex-Maldives President Nasheed offers help in Sivarasa Anojan case\n\nFormer Maldivian President Mohamed Nasheed has offered assistance in the case of Sri Lankan national Sivarasa Anojan, who faces a death sentence in Saudi Arabia.\n\nNasheed expressed his willingness when President\u2019s Counsel Faiszer Musthapha and President\u2019s Counsel Upul Kumarapperuma met him to discuss possible avenues for humanitarian intervention in Anojan\u2019s case.\n\nDuring the meeting, Nasheed told the two lawyers that while he considered Anojan\u2019s conduct \u201cdeplorable\u201d, he was willing to assist the Sri Lankan national on humanitarian grounds.\n\nThe meeting comes as Sri Lanka steps up legal and diplomatic efforts to seek relief for Anojan, following the enhancement of his sentence to death by a Saudi appellate court.\n\nForeign Minister Vijitha Herath told Parliament that Musthapha and Kumarapperuma had agreed to provide legal assistance in the case and travel to Saudi Arabia at their own expense. They are expected to coordinate with Anojan\u2019s legal representatives and relevant Saudi authorities to explore available legal remedies.\n\nThe Government has also said it will bear the legal costs associated with the case, as Anojan is a registered worker with the Sri Lanka Bureau of Foreign Employment."
  },
